umurmur
------------------------------------------
uMurmur is a minimalistic Mumble server primarily targeted to run on routers
with an open OS like OpenWRT. The server part of Mumble is called Murmur, hence
the name uMurmur.

Runtime requirements:
  cygwin-3.6.12-1
  libconfig15-1.8.3-1bl1
  libprotobuf-c1-1.5.2-1bl2
  libssl3-3.5.9-1

Build requirements:
(besides corresponding -devel packages)
  binutils-2.47-1
  cmake-4.4.5-1
  cygport-0.37.12-1
  gcc-core-14.4.0-1
  libconfig-devel-1.8.3-1bl1
  libprotobuf-c-devel-1.5.2-1bl2
  libssl-devel-3.5.9-1
  ninja-1.13.2-1

Canonical website:
  https://github.com/umurmur/umurmur

Canonical download:
  https://github.com/umurmur/umurmur/archive/refs/tags/v0.5.1.tar.gz

-------------------------------------------

Build instructions:
  1. unpack umurmur-0.5.1-X-src.tar.xz
  2. if you use setup to install this src package,
     it will be unpacked under /usr/src automatically
        % cd /usr/src
        % cygport ./umurmur-0.5.1-X.cygport all

This will create:
  /usr/src/umurmur-0.5.1-X-src.tar.xz
  /usr/src/umurmur-0.5.1-X.tar.xz

-------------------------------------------

Files included in the binary package:

(umurmur)
  /etc/defaults/etc/umurmur/umurmur.conf
  /etc/postinstall/umurmur.sh
  /etc/preremove/umurmur.sh
  /usr/bin/umurmurd.exe
  /usr/share/doc/Cygwin/umurmur.README
  /usr/share/doc/umurmur/AUTHORS
  /usr/share/doc/umurmur/CHANGELOG.md
  /usr/share/doc/umurmur/LICENSE
  /usr/share/doc/umurmur/README.md

